  "summary": "A canonical reading that traces redemptive history through God\u2019s covenants with creation, Abraham, Israel, David, and the new covenant.",
  "historical_context": "Covenant theology developed as a way of reading the Bible\u2019s storyline, especially within Reformed and confessional traditions, but it is rooted in the biblical text itself.",
  "ancient_near_east_context": "The theology takes seriously covenant forms familiar from the ancient Near East while insisting that the LORD\u2019s covenant is uniquely gracious and holy.",
  "literary_context": "It offers a big-picture lens for reading narrative, law, prophecy, Gospel, and epistle together.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Covenant theology highlights continuity and fulfillment across Scripture without collapsing distinct covenants into one undifferentiated category.",
